# Force LF on files that are consumed by Linux containers.
#
# Without this, a Windows working copy checks these out with CRLF. A shell script
# with CRLF line endings fails inside a Linux container with an obscure error
# ("bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M" or "no such file or directory"), because the
# carriage return is treated as part of the interpreter path. The same applies to
# anything a container parses line by line.
#
# `text eol=lf` normalises to LF in the repository AND on checkout, on every platform.

*.sh        text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
